diff --git a/help/C/templaros-index.page b/help/C/templaros-index.page
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..5c2d1a4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/C/templaros-index.page
@@ -0,0 +1,19 @@
+<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
+<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-or-later; Copyright 2026 TemplarOS contributors -->
+<page xmlns="http://projectmallard.org/1.0/" type="guide" id="index">
+  <info><desc>Search the shared TemplarOS file index</desc></info>
+  <title>FSearch for TemplarOS</title>
+  <p>Search results come from the shared file index. The notice reports their generation
+    and each folder's freshness. Manage indexed folders in Settings, under File Index.</p>
+  <p>Use words or quoted phrases, file: or folder:, size: comparisons and dm: or
+    datemodified: with ISO8601 dates. A term containing / searches paths. Sort by name,
+    path, size or modified time.</p>
+  <p>Several terms use AND. Additional terms filter the retained results of the longest
+    term; the notice states how many results were retained. This is not a complete
+    search beyond that retained limit.</p>
+  <p>Regex, wildcards, OR, NOT, exclusions, content:, exact and case-sensitive modes,
+    the Search in Path toggle, and type or extension sorting are unsupported. These
+    requests show a message. For paths, use a term containing /.</p>
+  <p>Select All includes every retained row, including rows beyond the visible page.
+    If a page becomes stale, the view refreshes and an incomplete selection is cleared.</p>
+</page>
